course: dictionary
lesson: 14575
title: One word, two meanings: pipeline
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pipeline is a long line of pipes that carries oil, gas or water over long distances, often under the ground or across the sea. «The gas pipeline runs under the sea.» Here the clues are gas and runs under the sea, so pipeline means pipes.
explain: Pipeline has a second meaning in a phrase. «A new playground is in the pipeline.» There are no pipes here. In the pipeline means the playground is being planned or prepared, and it will come soon.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. Look for clues: if the sentence talks about oil, gas or water moving along, think pipes. If it talks about plans or things coming soon, think of the phrase in the pipeline. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: A pipeline is a long line of pipes.
fact: Oil and gas pipelines can cross whole countries and even run under seas.
fact: «In the pipeline» means being planned or prepared, coming soon.
fact: In computing, a pipeline is a series of steps that data passes through.
fact: A good check: put your meaning into the sentence. «A new library is in the pipeline» still makes sense if you think of it as being planned.
exercise: «The oil pipeline carries oil across the desert.» What does pipeline mean here? | A road for cars | A group of friends | A type of shoe | *A long line of pipes that carries oil
exercise: «A new skate park is in the pipeline.» What does in the pipeline mean? | Finished and closed last year | *Being planned, coming soon | Made of metal | Lost under the ground
exercise: In computing, data moves along a pipeline. What is a pipeline in this sense? | *A series of steps that data passes through | A line of pipes under the sea | A pet fish | A long rope
test: Ruby says the new bridge is in the pipeline, so it must be made of pipes. What does in the pipeline really mean? | *Being planned or prepared, coming soon | Lost under the river | Made of metal pipes | Finished last year
test: «Gas flows through the pipeline to the city.» Which meaning fits best, and why? | A shoe: gas is worn on the feet | Plans: gas can be planned, so it means in the pipeline | *Pipes: gas flows through them, so it must be a line of pipes | A group of friends who share gas
exam: In «The new gas pipeline runs under the sea», which clue tells you pipeline means pipes? | The word new | The word the | *The words gas and runs under the sea | Nothing, it is only a guess
